        "original_id": "46e44b58-69c3-5c26-9d3d-a3995e7b0aed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- Films: The Little Mermaid, The Strongest Man in the World, Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, The Prince and the Pauper\n- People: H. Lee Peterson, Kurt Russell\n- Places: Medfield College\n- Roles: assistant editor, lead film editor\n\nFacts:\n- The Strongest Man in the World is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- The Little Mermaid is a 1989 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was an assistant editor for The Little Mermaid.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, and Home on the Range.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for the Mickey Mouse short film The Prince and the Pauper.",
